WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:02.420
On this wonderful day,

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.120
when all of you are ready to graduate, the Empire...

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.220
...has great expectations for all of you.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.320
With your youthful vigor, we hope you will be able to break open this long-fought war...

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.850
...and grasp victory with your hands.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.860
We expect nothing but your best-

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.580
C-Commandant!
We expect nothing but your best-

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.430
C-Commandant!

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.460
Commandant...

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.250
We're in the middle of a ceremony here.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.240
The emperor...

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.340
The emperor has...

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.340
...signed a ceasefire!

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:30.590
Ceasefire!

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.420
It's a notification of the ceasefire!

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.540
"A few days ago, the Empire"

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.800
"signed a ceasefire treaty with the Republic of Frost."

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.850
"As a consequence, the state of
national emergency has been lifted,"

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.190
"and all subjects of the Empire should immediately prepare for"

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.560
"the rebuilding of the Empire."

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.750
" -- From the Imperial Commander-in-Chief"

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:47.580
Wait!
" -- From the Imperial Commander-in-Chief"

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:47.770
Wait!

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.110
Why did this happen all of a sudden?

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:50.860
Ceasefire? How come?

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.830
Cease... fire?

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.310
Just like that...

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:01.700
Then...

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.150
Why didn't it... happen earlier?

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.100
A long war took place.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.630
The "blood calls out for blood" war with the Republic...

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.830
...left many deep scars throughout the lands of the Empire.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.790
Three years after the ceasefire, the "Thin Ice Treaty",

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:15.950
...starvation...

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:17.420
...epidemics...

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.060
...and soldiers turning into bandits...

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:21.620
This...

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:26.270
...was another war known as "war damages".

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.260
Shit... a tank...

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.440
I think you'd call this...

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.670
...a bandit's fortress rather than a dam.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:37.580
You're right.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.360
Okay, this should be good.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.910
Mr. Four-Eyes sure seems to be calm.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:45.370
Our mission is to investigate and report,

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.910
not to lay siege to the dam.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.440
Prepare for castle siege!

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:53.850
Crush them!

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.480
"Crush them"?

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.230
We're dealing with tanks here!

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.570
They bring disorder to society!

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.050
Slay-evil-immediately!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:04.380
Anyway, shouldn't we head over to investigate the damage?

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:13.470
Wait for me!

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.430
Okay!

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:16.360
Large asparagus salad, here you go.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.390
If you're looking for a job, sorry.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.010
No one can afford to hire you around here.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.250
That's some impressive food gobbling.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.430
Is that enough for you?

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:42.250
And here I was, thinking we'd have better food to eat after the war was over.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:44.910
See that place over there?

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:46.800
That dam.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:51.220
Since the war, this place hasn't changed much because of them.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:55.880
The bad guys just keep on gathering over there.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:01.020
A tank squad called Grauwolf bummed over to this place a year ago.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.950
They made the dam their fort and began raiding.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.080
We wanted to kick them out,

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.580
but against a tank, we can't do anything...

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.120
Another bowl, please.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.250
You're my kind of guy!

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.560
You can have all the green leaves you want!

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:23.050
Excuse us!

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.790
Umm, LT...

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.410
We're doing an undercover investigation,

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.680
so it's better if we do this in a more clandestine manner...

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:29.610
That's absurd!

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.570
Honorable soldiers acting in secret? Nonsense!

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.140
A soldier should always-

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.080
You guys soldiers from the capital?

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.530
Ah, pleased to meet you.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:52.710
We are from State Section III of the Imperial Army-

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.830
What is happening?

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:57.010
A shell...

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.580
...from a 65mm tank cannon.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:05.800
They're here...

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:14.610
Sorry, Mr. Mayor...

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.460
I couldn't hear you over the cannon noise.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:20.460
I'm not lying.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.300
We don't have any more provisions left in this village to spare.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.620
I didn't say "spare us";

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:25.880
I said "GIVE US"!

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.690
Should we give him another shot, lieutenant?

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:31.450
How many times do I have to say this until you get it?

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.440
Call me "Wolf"!

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.250
Wolf? What a joke!

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.120
You're just an ape from the mountains!

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:40.990
We're the Imperial Army S.S. III Pumpkin Scissors platoon!

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:45.910
We regard you as a war aggravator
and will proceed to remove you from the village!

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:47.670
Pumpkin Scissors?

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:49.810
I've heard of them before.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.680
They're a unit founded in the capital
whose purpose is to provide war relief efforts.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:55.100
Relief?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.590
Ready a K-3 round.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.790
We'll meet again, Pumpkin Scissors!

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.320
What? A blank shot?

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:37.430
That scared the hell out of us...

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:38.770
They ran away!

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.070
Halt-

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:39.600
There, there, LT.
Halt-

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:40.770
There, there, LT.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.440
Calm down a bit.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.380
Yes, especially now that they've retreated!

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.630
A blank?!

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:48.600
You can only go so far when insulting someone-

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.320
Is it raining or something?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.030
No, not really.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:57.910
That's unusual.

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:00.070
For this to happen twice in the same day-

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.370
To take on a tank like that...

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.170
...that's not something a normal person should be doing.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:12.330
What'll we do?

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:15.840
Their reinforcements from the capital might be headed here as early as tomorrow.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:17.530
No one's coming.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:22.090
There's no way they'd send reinforcements.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.400
That's strange...

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:36.320
They have one tank and at least thirty soldiers...

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:40.020
How has a big gang like this gone unnoticed all this time?

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.660
Hunks, I've heard!

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:42.870
You sent your men to that dam?!

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.300
Stekkin, prepare some tea for the head of Section I.
You sent your men to that dam?!

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:47.550
Stekkin, prepare some tea for the head of Section I.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:48.430
Yes, sir.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.620
Pull your investigation team out of there right now!

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.600
Don't touch Grauwolf!

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:02.180
Sorry, this is the only thing I can offer.

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:03.290
Ah, it's okay.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:04.710
Given the times, we know.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.180
You look pretty cute.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:10.410
Hey, you guys are pretty good!

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:11.870
You know...

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:15.310
...I thought you guys were just a public-relations gang for the big wigs,

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.740
but you guys sure surprised me!

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.320
Ah, thanks...

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:22.620
Those bandits ran away just after seeing you guys!

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.190
War relief unit...
Those bandits ran away just after seeing you guys!

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:25.710
War relief unit...

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.780
I am 2nd Lieutenant Alice L. Malvin.

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:34.290
What is your name?

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.680
Randel... Oland...

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:39.590
You're a war veteran, right?

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:43.640
So I was right.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:44.780
What's your rank?

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:46.190
Corporal.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.580
Do not worry.

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:50.210
I'm not looking at you as if you were one of those bandits.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:53.440
Your eyes look a lot like Piro's.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:54.770
Piro?

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.140
The horse I care for at home.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.920
I wanted to see your eyes to be sure.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.250
I had a cold chill on the back of my neck when I walked past you earlier.

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:08.180
There's always something unusual when I experience that.

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:09.820
I felt it when Piro was born...

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.960
...and also when I was promoted to 2nd Lieutenant.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.510
That must mean it's something good.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:16.850
Not always.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.960
I felt it when my grandfather passed away...

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:22.440
...the same with Piro's parents.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:24.420
Bad things happen more often.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:28.210
However, I'm pleased.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:33.720
It seems meeting you was a fortuitous fate for me, Corporal.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.990
Ah, yes, yes, what kind of unit were you in, Corporal?

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:41.550
Mistress!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:47.670
What's going on?!

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:48.610
I don't know!

00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:49.530
Everyone suddenly-

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:50.290
The doctor!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.250
Get the doctor!

00:10:58.280 --> 00:10:59.960
A volatile tactical chemical agent...

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:01.080
Kirsche-3.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:02.190
What?!

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:04.550
A K-3 chemical round.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:08.160
It was that blank they fired?!

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.180
Grauwolf is just a common name given to them.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:18.670
Their official name is 903-CTT.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:19.870
CTT?

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:23.220
Short for Chemical Tactics Troop.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:26.450
Kirsche-3 was already ready for operational use?

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:30.750
Excuse me, what's Kirsche-3?

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.970
A tactical poison that disperses in the air.

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:38.110
It has no effect on people with strong immune systems,

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.690
but for those that don't...

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:42.380
...they will have trouble staying conscious and will experience fevers within five or six hours.

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:44.220
Their bodies will cease to function properly...

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:47.610
...and will die if they don't receive the vaccine within twenty hours.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:49.800
Right?

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:50.620
Right.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:52.850
It's a weapon that violates the International Treaty.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:57.350
However, the Empire has created a number of these units.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:11:59.720
The "Invisible 9"...

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.910
So it wasn't just a rumor, eh?

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.850
903 was Krankheit Jäger,

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:07.390
otherwise known as
"the medics who scatter the ashes of death".

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:09.710
It was a forbidden move the Empire took;

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:11.600
their existence must not be known to the public.

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:13.140
So, in other words,

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:18.000
"903 does not exist" and
"we can't send reinforcements to a dam with nothing there".

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.760
A damn village is a small price to pay for this!

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.650
Oh my god, no, Mer-kun!

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:29.140
You can't bite heads lightly!

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.590
You call this biting lightly?!

00:12:30.590 --> 00:12:32.270
I can feel it going into my skull!

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:36.270
There's only one doctor so...

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:40.980
But this village is far better off than others because, at least, we have one.

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:44.170
Oh yeah, the vaccine!

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:45.140
What?

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:49.140
If they used a tactical poison, they must possess the vaccine.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:51.890
Hey, uhh, careful with what you say.

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:53.580
If Lieutenant Spearhead hears this-

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:54.500
I heard it!

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.580
Prepare for castle siege!

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:57.810
That's reckless!

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:59.340
You'll die in vain!

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:01.960
When you see people suffering...

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:03.720
When you see evil greedily preying upon others...

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:05.920
...do you not feel anything?

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.820
Do you really not feel anything?

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:13.600
Corporal, aren't you the one that is hiding
your true feelings and letting them waste away?

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.500
Does anyone have a map of the dam?

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:19.830
And bring us some light!

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:22.440
Lamps, torches, bring everything there is!

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:25.440
When I first heard it...

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:27.970
...I felt my heart skip a beat.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.970
War relief...

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:36.200
The problem is still that tank...

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:37.710
Indeed...

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.850
I'll take care of the tank.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:40.630
Corporal...

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:43.260
This dam is one that consists of multiple reservoirs, right?

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:47.270
Their positions are located in the area between the first and second dams.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.310
If you can discharge the water from
the first dam and flood that whole area...

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:53.940
The tank won't be able to move because of all the mud!

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:54.860
Yeah.

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:57.240
"To take on a tank is not something a normal person should be doing."

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.650
I remember someone saying that, right?

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.400
Yes, not a normal person.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.310
I haven't asked for your unit's name, yet.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:12.110
901-ATT.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:14.170
Come on, we don't have time.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:16.720
Wolf!

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:18.290
Reinforcements from the capital are here!

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:19.320
What?

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:20.840
You're kidding me.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.400
There're a lot of 'em.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.670
They're bluffing.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.220
You guys go take care of 'em.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.230
Yes, sir.

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:33.510
They didn't desert the village?

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:44.150
Great... why is the easygoing S.S. III
doing something like this?

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:46.690
You're the one who came up with this idea, Oreld.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.220
C'mon, c'mon, what's the matter?!

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.660
We'll make Swiss cheese out of ya!

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:53.470
Hey, don't you think our cover is blown?

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:57.830
Even if it's blown, it's not like they can let
themselves split up their manpower any more.

00:14:58.020 --> 00:14:59.370
This is what you call tactics.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.160
But, man, Machs...

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:03.040
What?

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:06.170
The other group might've gotten it easy...

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:10.940
How is it?

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:11.890
It's useless.

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:13.760
It's impossible with tools like this.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:17.490
Step back please.

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:28.030
Lieutenant, you go secure the vaccine.

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:31.260
I'll take care... of the floodgate...

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:34.250
Will you be all right by yourself?

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:37.450
H-Hey... Corporal!

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:42.470
Go... already...

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:45.060
O-Okay... Be careful...

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.260
That blue light isn't leaving my eyes...

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:07.680
So cold... and dusky...

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:09.810
...like a will o' the wisp...

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:15.680
He... might've been... some monstrous person...

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:22.670
He did it?

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.830
W-What happened?!

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:27.830
The gate...

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.100
The water's flooding over here...

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:38.200
They're trying to limit our mobility, huh?

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:39.480
This is fun...

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:41.100
Get the tank ready.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:42.990
We can still move right now.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.070
Roger!

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:53.690
I can't believe I'm acting like a burglar...

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:55.640
Let's see, the vaccine...

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:08.010
Damn it!

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.430
This is like dog paddling...

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.170
On top of that, this visibility...

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:13.910
One false move and we'll fall down the dam...

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:17.970
What's that...

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.230
What's the matter?

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:22.940
I think I see a ghost or something...

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:27.190
A night blue lantern light?!

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.320
Ready a strong acid round!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.890
He'll melt down to his bones if he gets hit by this!

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:40.990
Hurry up!

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:42.660
I'm sorry!

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:47.370
He disappeared...

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:48.390
Find him!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.130
Damn it, where'd he go?

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:54.260
Damn, visibility sucks!

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:04.180
Fall back!

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:05.940
Don't let him come near us!

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.060
Y-Yes, sir!

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:12.480
W-What the hell is he?!

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:18.130
"They will come forth along with the blue will o' the wisps..."

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:22.370
The 901 Anti-Tank Troopers...

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:25.450
Then he's a Gespenst Jäger?!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.700
Yeah, he's one of us...

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.710
The troopers that disregard their own lives!

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.850
Damn it, we're stuck!

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:37.330
Hurry!

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:38.220
Y-Yes, sir!

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.060
Eat this!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:50.090
You think you can block that with just a coat?

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:51.560
...what the...

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:59.060
Stop... s-s-stop!

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:05.300
They usually stop, don't they?

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:05.950
Calm down!

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:10.520
Let go!

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.750
You monster, let go!

00:19:35.930 --> 00:19:38.210
A point-blank shot without any regard for self-preservation...

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:42.620
A battle style just like what they say, eh, 901?

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:47.620
What's the matter? Shoot me already!

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:50.020
Ah, I see...

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:52.930
Shoot me and the vaccine falls with me, too!

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:55.790
Come on, shoot me!

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:58.090
Shoot me, shoot me, shoot back at me!

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:00.470
You're supposed to be on our side.

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:04.030
What's the point in working your ass off for them?

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:08.180
War relief... dream on!

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:14.140
Damn girl!

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:26.590
I haven't... asked your name yet...

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:31.470
I'm Lieutenant Wolmav...

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:35.340
No... we don't have names...

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:40.560
Call me... Wolf...

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:47.040
Wolf got defeated...

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:47.640
Shit!

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:48.530
Run!

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:49.890
Hey! Hold it!

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.000
Th-Thank God!

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.590
No more!

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:55.720
I'm not doing this anymore!

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.780
S.S. III isn't easygoing at all!

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:22.230
That's an awful scald you have.

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:23.300
Are you all right?

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:24.260
Yeah.

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:25.820
I'm used to it.

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:28.730
I don't know what you're musing about,

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:30.120
but the sun's about to rise.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.750
Shape up already! Come on!

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:32.670
Ah...

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:36.230
You saved the villagers.

00:21:38.720 --> 00:21:41.500
It's only a small part of the whole picture,

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:44.570
but this is the war relief that you've accomplished.

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:52.680
But, really, your outfit sure is horrible.

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:55.760
All right! I'll get you a new outfit!

00:23:30.890 --> 00:23:34.060
Mer-kun, they say a new Corporal is coming today!

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:36.220
I'll finally have an underling!

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:37.570
I wonder what kind of person he is!

00:23:37.570 --> 00:23:39.520
Come to me already, my underling!

00:23:39.820 --> 00:23:41.920
Next time, "War Relief Unit"!

00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:44.110
Come get us if you're not scared!
